{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aegis/1491077-tc-aegis-myths-beings-musings","id":1491077,"title":"[TC Aegis] Myths beings musings","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aegis"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-22T22:29:08-07:00","id":1491077,"title":"[TC Aegis] Myths beings musings","content":"So we DO NOT know anything concrete about <b>TC Aegis</b> era 'Bronze Age S-F' or it's fundamentals, even. But let's filled the long months waiting for the <b>Aegis</b> to finish with our fan musings how various Mythical beings can work in the <b>Trinity Continuum</b> world of Bronze Age. \ud83d\ude0e<br /> <br /> Here is great source for Greek myths wiki in general - <a href=\"https://www.theoi.com/greek-mythology/nymphs.html\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.theoi.com/greek-mythology/nymphs.html</a><br /> <br /> I'm coming with assumption that general templates divide is this:<br /> <br /> <b>Talents / Daredevils / Squires = Heroes<br /> Novas / Stalwarts = Gods / Demigods<br /> Psiads (/Psions?) = Wizards and mystics</b><br /> <br /> Starting topic with various...<br /> <br /> <b>NYMPHS</b><br /> Nymphs are various lesser goddesses, 'youngest' in godly family. They are Quantum users, limited always to having maximum Quantum 1 and cannot pass beyond that. However, they are very hard to detect even as Quantum users - they have +3 bonus on Clash of Wills to get to overpower them in detection. \ud83d\ude0e","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-23-2022, 02:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-22T23:32:45-07:00","id":1491079,"title":"","content":"I'd equate Novas/Stalwarts/Superiors/Sub-Aberrants with demigods, not gods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-22T23:56:43-07:00","id":1491080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aegis/1491077-tc-aegis-myths-beings-musings?p=1491079#post1491079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd equate Novas/Stalwarts/Superiors/Sub-Aberrants with demigods, not gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>But what about then Heroes Demigods? \ud83e\udd14 They are most popular in Greek Myths. Even more - it's almost definition that Hero = Demigod...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-23-2022, 03:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T08:58:09-07:00","id":1491095,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d actually say stalwarts are demigods and novas are gods. Novas can do some pretty insane things, whereas demigods\u2019 powers are, classically speaking, <i>much</i> more restrained.<br /> <br /> Your Nymph idea is pretty good, too. I like the idea of them being the earliest form of Quantum-users humanity\u2019s ever had. I\u2019d not make them gender-specific, though. Maybe call the females Nymphs, but the males Fauns?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T09:32:45-07:00","id":1491100,"title":"","content":"I think those &quot;magical creatures&quot; will be people from weird places, as happens to the atlanteans and the people from the great bahobahb.<br /> <br /> It was said the characters will not be the gods, but proabably heroes (Odiseus), demigods (Achiles) and magicians (Circe).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T10:50:27-07:00","id":1491104,"title":"","content":"Well, that eliminates the idea of ancient novas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T11:09:14-07:00","id":1491108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aegis/1491077-tc-aegis-myths-beings-musings?p=1491104#post1491104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, that eliminates the idea of ancient novas.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. It makes you characters not being Zeus, but it wont mean the general population wont think he is a god.<br /> <br /> From the view of a normal person, specially one from the bronze age, a person that can shoot lightining bolts that can kill an elephant is as powerful as a god can be, same for most powers a nova can use at Q2 or 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T14:09:08-07:00","id":1491122,"title":"","content":"Stalwarts can\u2019t do Zeus; novas <i>can</i>. As of 2028, somebody like Antaeus, with a Quantum of a 6, is basically the god of the wilderness. Now, imagine Antaeus at the close of the Aberrant War, having several decades as a nova under his belt. He may as well be a Greek titan. Not omnipotent, not unbeatable, but <i>awfully</i> close.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 08-23-2022, 07:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T14:14:23-07:00","id":1491124,"title":"","content":"I don't think it would take much to tweak the stalwart rules to be able to handle Zeus. The main thing lacking, I suspect, is Scale. And that's easily addressed, I think: for Nova style \u201cstalwarts\u201d, let them take Dynamic gifts that grant Scale multiple times to gain increased Scale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-23-2022, 05:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-23T16:13:27-07:00","id":1491139,"title":"","content":"Me? I\u2019d prefer Talents and...something new, like they appear to be doing in TC Aether! Maybe half-human/half-alien characters? Good ol\u2019 fashion giants, no bells or whistles attached? Playable aliens, maybe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T10:22:11-07:00","id":1491212,"title":"","content":"I tend to agree with the people who think gods and things won't be modeled in Aegis as a playable character type. Beyond just balance and things, if the game is set in the time of the Trojan war you're not dealing with Greek gods, but Mycenaean ones and we don't really know a ton about them.<br /> <br /> Like a lot of the same names appear, but Poseidon is the leader of the Gods, not Zeus, and he's more (or equally?) famous for causing earthquakes. Aphrodite hasn't been fully integrated into the pantheon yet from her likely Phoenician origins as Astarte. Dionysus is an extremely fringe wine cult figure who threatens orderly society and is more associated with madness than party fun times. Hades <i>seemingly</i> doesn't exist. Demeter and Persephone might be wives of Poseidon. Persephone <i>might</i> be the goddess of death and the underworld. Hermes and Pan might still be the same god (I forget when we think they started to separate).<br /> <br /> Greek mythology is wildly fluid over time and we tend to project the later shape of things backwards and assume it was always that way. <br /> <br /> It is waaaaay easier to just deal with the semi-historical heroes and people from a pretty amazing period of history than tangle with the rats nest of nearly unrecognizable Mycenaean mythology. Also, while this isn't a huge danger for Mycenaean or Ancient Greek religion, trying to mash real world religions into game systems/settings can easily become wildly offensive. I remember someone commented that the 1st Edition of Scion's take on Zoroastrian and Hindu pantheons managed to be blasphemous to followers of both religions, which was impressive considering neither faith has a concept of blasphemy.<br /> <br /> The same holds true for &quot;the gods were aliens!&quot; which would be very genre appropriate, but treads really close to a lot of the problematic issues around most ancient alien conspiracy theories.<br /> <br /> Let the gods be myths and stories to explain what is happening in the world. People might worship Poseidon at a cave that earthquakes seem to originate from and a voice demands sacrifices of metals and food, but it's because there is a crashed alien spaceship with amphibious horselike aliens inside, every time they run an engine test they cause an earthquake, and they're trying to get supplies so they can fix their ship. The aliens don't have anything to do with Poseidon, but the locals assume they do because they're trying to make sense of something they don't understand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T10:40:00-07:00","id":1491217,"title":"","content":"....amphibious horse-like aliens? Space seahorses? That...is <i>amazing</i>. I am not being sarcastic, I am not being derisive, I am stating genuine joy at such a wonderfully bizarre idea. Consider this idea stolen!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T10:50:22-07:00","id":1491218,"title":"","content":"There are 4 main options to bring &quot;gods&quot; to the game not being our characters:<br /> The first is the gods are aliens that may mate or impersonate or dominate humans pretending to be gods (they are something between Marvel gods and Stargate Goauld).<br /> The second is we have alien &quot;gods&quot;, but they are not human at all, they are Mythos material and our heroes are the humans standing against them (think something Krull).<br /> The third is the gods are the a few of the stalwarts that become so powerful they become true novas (or psiads that reached Proxy level) (Something close to Xena and Hercules tv series, but based in scientific premices).<br /> The forth is the gods are not real, they are based in and the stories of Zeus as described in the mythlogy are not real, but just stories told so many times its scale grew out of its original proportions (you can lift a big rock, but as the stories were told over time that rock become a montain), the ones that inspired the stories are long dead and our heros are their descendents (if not by blood, by concept).<br /> <br /> I am in favor of the 4th because we dont need ancient Novas, we need just powerful characters that inpire local stories, wth different heroes inspireing different stories all around the world instead of the Monomyth that you have with novas capable of moving the moon and things like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T11:01:36-07:00","id":1491221,"title":"","content":"I would also point out that this is Trinity continuum, not Scion. High Fidelity to mythology is something that the latter does; it need not be something for \u00c6gis to concern itself with too much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T11:45:19-07:00","id":1491225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aegis/1491077-tc-aegis-myths-beings-musings?p=1491221#post1491221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would also point out that this is Trinity continuum, not Scion. High Fidelity to mythology is something that the latter does; it need not be something for \u00c6gis to concern itself with too much.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but it <i>would</i> be fulfilling, at least to me, to have my group I\u2019m GMing say, \u201cGreek myth? That was loosely based on <i>us</i>.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T12:45:28-07:00","id":1491230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aegis/1491077-tc-aegis-myths-beings-musings?p=1491221#post1491221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would also point out that this is Trinity continuum, not Scion. High Fidelity to mythology is something that the latter does; it need not be something for \u00c6gis to concern itself with too much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, and stuff like &quot;These ancient gods were actually aliens/some guys with powers/time travellers wowing primitive people with tech!&quot; is a pretty common sci-fi trope, it's just one with some pretty bad baggage that easily slips into problematic territory. \u00c6gis will probably be fine since it is so distant from any extant cultures and religions even if it goes that route.<br /> <br /> High Fidelity to mythology seems to be a route Scion 2E took after not doing that in 1E and stumbling into some pretty offensive territory. I'd really hate to see TC accidentally do the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4270,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","user":"literatzi","date":". 08-24-2022, 04:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T12:57:03-07:00","id":1491231,"title":"","content":"There is also a comment somewhere that Aegis will not be about the &quot;Golden Era&quot; when the gods walk over earth, but about a later era, one of heroes and monsters, not gods and titans.<br /> <br /> I would say one taking place in the time of the Illiad and Odisey, or by the time of the Argonauts is the best option. You have the &quot;distant presence&quot; of the gods guiding adventureas and wars with blessings and dreams, but not poping in the battle field, and at same time you have the guy taking 12 years to complete a 2 weeks trip and ending up in islands out of any map.<br /> <br /> Another thing I would love to see, that fits the theme AND the style of play (action heroes) is something similar to Xena and Hercules TV series... I hope I can play them with Aegis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 08-24-2022, 04:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T15:05:30-07:00","id":1491246,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d prefer new character types. Something new. Gone, by the time period of Adventure!, but once quite prevalent. Giants! Literal giants! No bells, no whistles, no funny weird powers, just <i>giants</i>, in their last great hurrah!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T15:18:35-07:00","id":1491248,"title":"","content":"Giants, Satyrs, Nymphs, etc etc etc. They are all possible people from strange places, and so they are possible characters for sure.<br /> <br /> Under Aliens Skies have a set of rules on how to balance different species, in the case aliens. Worth the reading to have some ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T15:31:54-07:00","id":1491251,"title":"","content":"Something like Xena and Hercules? Sounds good to me. Bear in mind but those shows played rather fast and loose with the mythology. That said, I think that the best way to handle that would be to leave the actual mythology out of it entirely; Focus entirely on original characters.<br /> <br /> I don't mind there being giants, or saters, or herpes, and so on and so forth, in the setting. <i>Possibly</i> even allow heroes, magicians, or demigods who are also a non-human type. But the whole idea behind \u00c6gis is the heroes, magicians, and demigods. I would be extremely disappointed if it <i>didn't</i> center around them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T21:44:26-07:00","id":1491274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aegis/1491077-tc-aegis-myths-beings-musings?p=1491218#post1491218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are 4 main options to bring &quot;gods&quot; to the game not being our characters:<br /> The first is the gods are aliens that may mate or impersonate or dominate humans pretending to be gods (they are something between Marvel gods and Stargate Goauld).<br /> (...)<br /> The forth is the gods are not real, they are based in and the stories of Zeus as described in the mythlogy are not real, but just stories told so many times its scale grew out of its original proportions (you can lift a big rock, but as the stories were told over time that rock become a montain), the ones that inspired the stories are long dead and our heros are their descendents (if not by blood, by concept).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a bit Ancient Aliens nerd - and we HAVE Aliens Races in <b>Trinity Continuum</b> - that I would like, at least in part, for the 'aliens WERE our gods'. In at least few examples - rest can easily be 'Hercules and Xena -like Talents tales spinning out of proportions'.<br /> <br /> In Trinity we already things like ( from <b>TC Aether</b> ) <i>Three Prongs</i> in India 'worshiping' alien spaceship as demon/god. We have literal Martian cults in the same book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T06:54:04-07:00","id":1491295,"title":"","content":"I imagine the Doyen <i>looovve</i> posing as deities, though something tells me they\u2019d give only a cursory glance at the beliefs they\u2019re commandeering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T07:27:32-07:00","id":1491296,"title":"","content":"20k years ago or so the Doyen were not interested in humanity, so probably they will not be the big bad aliens of later. <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Their interest in Earth comes just after they deal with the Ascendency</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> But some aliens would fit nicelly as Gods or Titans. While I think we could use some alien astronauts as gods in other settings, I think the greek gods and myths are more human than others, and so the gods should not be too alien.<br /> <br /> My real hope is we could have people form weird places long traped on a much less powerful earth than theirs, or new arrivals shaking the status quo of the current gods, or all kind of bizare options that can come from the strange places we have. It would be far more greek myths than a ship full of aliens.<br /> <br /> A ship full of aliens fits better on the pyramid building peoples... I thing I watch too much History Chanel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T07:38:49-07:00","id":1491299,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Ancient Aliens is a favorite of mine, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T16:16:55-07:00","id":1491365,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't mind ancient astronauts. That said, subvert the usual portrayal of them by having whatever advances they cause in human civilization an inadvertent side effect of the humans use of the gifts granted to them by the aliens arrival.<br /> <br /> And let's not use the ascendancy again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T19:14:33-07:00","id":1491388,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ll be happy if I get some giants. They\u2019re part of essentially every mythology on earth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T20:56:57-07:00","id":1491392,"title":"","content":"I play <b>AC Valhalla</b> lately. It's set (mainly) in England of 870s CE. There is there quest based on Beowulf poem. Killings there are made by very large, autistic human as Grendel and his overprotective mother that poisoned them with a mold from the cave he was raised. To say that it was a bit underwhelming is understatement. Hearing rumors in game then about Jotunns - Giants - I was hoping there at least about some aliens/first civilisation mutated people of very large sizes... \ud83e\udd14","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-26-2022, 12:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-26T09:09:40-07:00","id":1491426,"title":"","content":"Wow. How sad. Especially considering the importance jotnar play in pagan Norse religion.<br /> <br /> Now, I don\u2019t mean magical giants. I just mean gargantuan people, another branch of humanity, now gone extinct. <i>Homo gigantis</i>, or something similar. Something, by TC Aether, is almost gone from the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-02T04:59:36-07:00","id":1492151,"title":"","content":"With coming <b>TC Aegis</b>, I want to point you how <b>Assassin's Creed</b> series reinterprets mythologies in the context of its lore based on elements of SF and First Civilization - <b>Isu </b>\ud83d\ude2e Just change Isu for Aliens - and you got answers for Trinity Continuum. \ud83d\ude0e<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_pRZxai0snY\" data-code=\"_pRZxai0snY\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/_pRZxai0snY/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}